<title>UK: Novorossiisk oil port reopens, Tuapse still closed.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk oil port reopens, Tuapse still closed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea port of Novorossiisk, Russia's main outlet for crude oil exports, reopened on Thursday morning having been shut for a day and half, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port reopened at 0730 local time after high winds and a heavy swell forced its closure on Tuesday afternoon.</p>
<p>But the smaller Tuapse terminal remained closed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The source said that two tankers were at anchor waiting to load at the berth one at Novorossiisk, the only berth which can accommodate vessels of up to 140,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>A smaller tanker berthed at berth two this morning, while two more were waiting at anchor.</p>
<p>&quot;Loadings are running about a day behind schedule,&quot; the shipping source said.</p>
<p>The other Black Sea oil port of Odessa and Ventspils on the Baltic were reported to be operating normally.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5387</p>
